pp. For more details, see Publish site in Building a Site .      Clear the app cache. For more details, see Clearing the App Cache.    \nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-24\nValid as Of: 2024-07-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2553 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Condition Exclusion on Condition Record Level\nDescription: The exclusion indicator (KONP-KZNEP) that was maintained for a condition record is now considered during condition determination of the next condition types in a pricing procedure. To be able to use it, the following standard requirement formulas were changed:    Requirement formula 5 is now supported. It ensures that a condition type is only considered if the exclusion indicator was not set by a previously found condition record.      Requirement formula 6 is now supported. It ensures that a condition type is only considered if the exclusion indicator was not set to X by a previously found condition record.      Requirement formula 2 was enhanced to not only check if the pricing indicator (KOMP-PRSFD) equals X or B, but to also check that the exclusion indicator was not set by a previously found condition record.      See Condition Exclusion and Supported Standard Pricing Exits.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-28\nValid as Of: 2024-07-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2554 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Consider Cost Conditions as External Conditions\nDescription: Condition types with data source other than Condition Technique are considered as external conditions where the condition rate must be passed by the caller if it is to be considered.   Now we also consider cost condition types without an access sequence with condition category Q (Cost) and G (Internal price) as external conditions as the data f